    "body": "## Summary\n- add authenticated realtime notification preferences for chat and review events\n- persist muted realtime types with Flyway V20 and user-scoped uniqueness\n- keep every notification durably stored in the inbox even when its realtime popup is muted\n- keep lifecycle, dispute, verification and other critical notification types non-mutable\n- expose GET/PUT `/notifications/preferences`\n- add notification-centre switches in the web app\n- cover muted realtime delivery and critical-type validation in service tests\n- document persistence, privacy and delivery semantics\n\n## Safety / architecture\n- preferences are always scoped to the authenticated principal\n- critical transactional/safety notifications cannot be muted\n- muting affects WebSocket delivery only; durable notification history is never discarded\n- preference replacement uses a deterministic bulk delete before insert to avoid uniqueness/flush ordering problems\n\n## Validation\nRun full API Maven verify, frontend lint/build, Flyway/PostgreSQL migration checks and existing runtime/payment smoke gates. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
